From 064bfc5c00b33d7cbdf05b574656ccccf4c32a44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:37:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S11 bool-pair-prune-fix: atomic post-RA prune + regression
 pins

The bool-pair post-RA prune un-skipped legs by OPERAND id instead of leg
Cmp DEST id, leaving both setcc emissions skipped while the And fell back
to a real andl over never-written boolean homes (half-pruned miscompile:
hits=1024/0 instead of 256/303 under CCC_NO_FOLDED_INDEX_LIVENESS=1).

Fix: record both leg dests in a CmpBoolPair struct (named fields replace
the 8-tuple that lost them) and remove dest1/dest2 on prune. Scan,
emission, tail-jmp, memset/idiom disjointness, i686 gate, and S06/fused/
fp-select exclusions all re-audited sound.

Tests: check_bool_pair_prune.sh (proven FAIL pre-fix / PASS post-fix in
both miscompile directions + fusion-disabled control), vecreg_map_liveout
+ vecreg_stencil_liveout S10 pins (proven i=64/128 pre-S10, i=512 post).
Full suite: build/clippy/cargo-test/fmt/corpus-739/bench-204/diff-57/
align/prune/tailjmp all green.
